Alembic migrations for config/titles.db.

The schema is defined in app/titledb/schema.py; titles.db is created, stamped and upgraded by
titledb.store.init_titledb(), called from db.init_db() exactly like ownfoil.db.

Create a revision (from anywhere, against a titles.db already at head — autogenerate diffs the
metadata against whatever your local file contains):

    alembic -c app/titledb/migrations/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "..."

titles.db is rebuilt from the titledb JSON only when the download changed or the locale did, so
a migration that adds a column needing JSON data must force a rebuild:

    op.execute("DELETE FROM meta WHERE key = 'imported_locale'")

There is no backup before migrating: titles.db is fully derivable from the downloaded JSON plus
custom_titles.json, and init_titledb() recreates it empty if anything goes wrong.
